>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Site-by-site g-xTB review of the preferred resonance form. Chose a localized Lewis representation for delocalized electrons within the same ligand. Re–N–O 171.39°, N–O 1.18663 Å, g-xTB N–O WBO 1.5754. The closed-shell assignment for this near-linear terminal ligand is N≡[O+], with metal formal charge +1 and total charge +0. Terminal ligand identity, the remaining graph and charge balance were checked; The original M–N–O angle, M–N and N–O distances, and WBO agree with documented NO⁺ controls matched by metal, formal state, NO count and ligand class. Localized 6 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths.

