>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. Pd(II) coordinates a C3H5 allyl anion. The other C34H30N3P ligand contains carbene and iminophosphorane groups, P41–N2 is about 1.65 Å; Charges cancel within P⁺–N⁻ and separately within endocyclic N⁺–C⁻. The frozen graph gives a compatible Lewis limiting form. Localized 34 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Checked each ligand's bond orders and formal charges against the input geometry. The atom order and coordinates of all 77 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 80 nonmetal covalent bonds: 77 within range, 2 outside range and 1 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 5–43 C-H 1.0928 Å, 9–46 C-H 1.0935 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

